  "replacement": "Sonya's letter from Troitsa, which had come as an answer to Nicholas' prayer, had a cause. The old countess thought more and more about marrying Nicholas to an heiress. She knew Sonya was the main obstacle, and Sonya's life in the countess' house had grown harder and harder, especially after a letter from Nicholas told of his meeting with Princess Mary at Bogucharovo. The countess never let a chance slip to make humiliating or cruel remarks about Sonya."
